## Coordinate Build and Query warehouse selectors

Context: The Lakehouse Settings panel exposed only the Query warehouse, so the
relationship between Build and Query compute was not visible. Query must use
Build by default and expose a separate selection only when an administrator
enables Lakehouse//RT.

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/settings.html
   Added read-only Build and conditional Query dropdowns to the Lakehouse SQL
   Warehouse tab and clarified the RT toggle.
2. src/front/static/config/js/settings.js
   Mirrored Build into a disabled Query selector by default, enabled only RT
   warehouses in query override mode, and cleared the override when RT is
   disabled.
3. src/back/objects/domain/SettingsService.py
   Required a distinct Query warehouse in RT mode and normalized non-RT saves
   to an empty override so reads fall back to Build.
4. tests/units/settings/test_delta_warehouse_config.py
   Added regression coverage for required, distinct, and cleared query
   overrides.
5. tests/units/api/test_ui_rendering.py,
   tests/units/front/test_settings_warehouse_split.py
   Added markup and JavaScript contracts for the coordinated selectors.
6. docs/architecture.md, docs/deployment.md, docs/get-started.md
   Documented the default mirroring and RT-enabled query override behavior.
7. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-10-build-query-warehouse-split-design.md,
   docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-10-build-query-warehouse-split.md
   Updated the approved design and plan with the corrected interaction.

