## Add a Settings toggle to disable CloudFetch

Context: Explorer searches on ontobricks-09x used the Lakehouse//RT query
warehouse and finished SQL in hundreds of milliseconds, then timed out in the
browser while CloudFetch retried downloads from
`us-west-2.storage.cloud.databricks.com` (`connection refused`). Admins needed
a global way to turn CloudFetch off without a redeploy.

Changes:

1. src/front/templates/settings.html
   Added an admin-only **Use CloudFetch** checkbox under Settings → Databricks.
2. src/front/static/config/js/settings.js
   Hydrated the checkbox from `/settings/current` and persisted both on and
   off through the shared Save handler.
3. src/back/objects/domain/SettingsService.py
   Exposed `use_cloud_fetch` in the current-config payload and saved it to
   global config (admin only).
4. src/api/routers/internal/settings.py
   Added `POST /settings/save-cloud-fetch`.
5. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaBase.py
   Passed the resolved CloudFetch flag into the Explorer/query SQL client.
6. docs/architecture.md, docs/get-started.md
   Documented the global CloudFetch setting and the Apps egress workaround.
7. tests/units/settings/test_cloud_fetch_toggle.py,
   tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_base.py,
   tests/units/api/test_ui_rendering.py,
   tests/units/settings/test_delta_warehouse_config.py
   Added contracts for persistence, UI wiring, and query-client propagation.

