## Isolate Databricks saves from unloaded Lakehouse controls

Context: Saving the global CloudFetch option succeeded, but the shared Settings
handler also validated the Lakehouse//RT Query warehouse before its dropdown
had been loaded. This produced a false "Select a Query SQL Warehouse" error
when saving from Settings → Databricks. The Query selector also restricted its
options to RT warehouses instead of presenting the Build selector's workspace
list.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/config/js/settings.js
   Tracks successful Query warehouse hydration and only persists that selection
   from the shared Save handler after its controls have loaded. Populates Query
   with all workspace warehouses except the selected Build warehouse.
2. tests/units/settings/test_cloud_fetch_toggle.py
   Added regression coverage ensuring a Databricks save does not validate an
   unloaded Lakehouse Query warehouse.
3. tests/units/front/test_settings_warehouse_split.py
   Added a contract for the shared Build/Query warehouse option list.
4. docs/get-started.md,
   docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-10-build-query-warehouse-split-design.md,
   docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-10-build-query-warehouse-split.md
   Documented Query list population and distinct warehouse validation.

